.Dd $Mdocdate: October 28 2026 $
.Dt PROTON-LAUNCHER 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm proton-launcher
.Nd download and start Windows games from Steam and your own games
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl v
.Op Ar command Op Ar arg ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
logs in to a Steam account, lists the Windows games it owns, downloads
them from Steam's content servers and starts them with
.Xr proton-openbsd 1 .
It also keeps a list of games that did not come from Steam.
It does not use or install Valve's Steam client: it talks to Steam's
servers directly, the way the open-source SteamKit2 library does.
.Pp
Without a command,
.Nm
shows a menu of installed games.
The commands are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm login Op Ar account
Log in.
.Nm
asks for the password and, if the account uses Steam Guard, for the
code from the email or the mobile app; a login can also be approved in
the mobile app.
Steam answers with a login token, which is saved in
.Pa login
in the data directory, readable only by the user.
The password is not saved.
.It Cm logout
Delete the saved login token.
.It Cm library
List the Windows games the account owns, with their app IDs.
.It Cm info Ar appid
Show a game's depots, which of them would be downloaded and why the others
are not, and the program Steam starts.
.It Cm install Ar appid
Download a game, or bring it up to date.
Only the Windows depots for 64-bit or any architecture, in English, that
the account owns are downloaded.
Files already present are checked chunk by chunk and kept when they are
correct, so an interrupted download resumes where it stopped.
Every chunk is verified with its SHA-1 hash.
.It Cm uninstall Ar appid
Delete a downloaded game.
Its wine prefix is kept.
.It Cm free Ar appid
Ask Steam to add a free game to the account.
.It Cm add Ar name Ar program.exe Op Ar arg ...
Add one of your own games under
.Ar name .
.It Cm remove Ar name
Remove a game added with
.Cm add
from the list.
.It Cm list
List the installed games.
.It Cm run Ar appid | name Op Ar arg ...
Start a game with
.Ic proton-openbsd run ,
in the game's own wine prefix
.Pq Pa prefixes/ Ns Ar appid
and working directory.
.It Cm menu
The interactive menu.
.El
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl a
.Cm ( info ,
.Cm install )
Log in anonymously instead, which gives access to Steam's freely
downloadable tools and dedicated servers.
.It Fl b Ar branch
.Cm ( info ,
.Cm install )
Use another branch than
.Dq public .
Branches with a password are not supported.
.It Fl j Ar threads
.Cm ( install )
Download with this many connections; the default is 8.
.It Fl v
Print debugging messages.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev PROTON_LAUNCHER_DIR
The data directory.
Defaults to
.Pa ${XDG_DATA_HOME:-~/.local/share}/proton-launcher .
.It Ev PROTON_PREFIX
If set, used as the wine prefix for every game.
.El
.Pp
.Xr proton-openbsd 1
reads its own variables, such as
.Ev PROTON_USE_WINED3D
and
.Ev PROTON_LOG .
.Sh FILES
In the data directory:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa login
The account name and Steam's login token.
.It Pa settings
Optional settings, one
.Dq key value
pair per line:
.Cm library_dir Ar dir
(where games are downloaded, default
.Pa steamapps/common ) ,
.Cm shared_prefix yes
(one wine prefix for all games),
.Cm proton Ar program
(instead of
.Xr proton-openbsd 1 ) .
.It Pa steamapps/ Ns Ar appid Ns Pa .info
What
.Cm install
recorded about a game: name, directory, program, arguments and working
directory.
It can be edited to start another program.
.It Pa games/ Ns Ar name
A game added with
.Cm add .
.It Pa prefixes/
The wine prefixes.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ proton-launcher login
$ proton-launcher library
$ proton-launcher install 1234560
$ proton-launcher run 1234560
$ proton-launcher add Mygame ~/games/mygame/mygame.exe -windowed
$ proton-launcher run Mygame
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr proton-openbsd 1
.Sh CAVEATS
Many games call the Steamworks API
.Pq Pa steam_api64.dll
at start and expect a running Steam client, which
.Nm
is not; such games usually exit at once or show an error.
Games without Steam DRM or Steamworks requirements run.
Anti-cheat systems are not supported.
.Pp
Only 64-bit Windows programs run on
.Ox .
.Pp
Downloads are not throttled and Steam's download regions are not
selectable.
